A flake is a first-trial failure followed by fixed rerun success. The first failure remains visible. Positive anchors must pass every trial; negative anchors must reject every trial; either violation fails the gate. Safety items permit no skip and no flake.

The fixture is a deterministic oracle only. It makes no claim about a real provider, people, or generalization. No product defaults, product locks, approval semantics, or scheduled automation are changed.
"},{"path":"harness/specs/rules/reliability-aggregation-boundary.md","content":"# Reliability aggregation boundary

- Reuse the Agent Dev benefit report; do not create a metrics platform.
- Keep trial-level missing, timeout, crashed, and skipped outcomes visible.
- Exclude incomplete cases from pass^k and pass@k denominators, while reporting raw and complete denominators.
- Never use a small sample to report PASS. k, minCases, and flake threshold are fixture configuration.
- pass^k is not pass@k.
- Flake does not erase the initial failure.
- Positive and negative anchors are hard gates. Safety required cases have zero skip and zero flake.
- The deterministic oracle is not evidence of provider behavior, human performance, or model generalization.
- Do not alter product defaults, product locks, approval semantics, permissions, dependencies, or automation.
